   }
  },
  {
   "id": "av2_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 878,
   "y": 538,
   "width": 74,
   "height": 15,
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100072,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700504,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "800",
   "originalText": "800",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "av2",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 660,
   "width": 761,
   "height": 97,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100073,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700511,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "This gives a key-value store built out of the log - and it fits the offset workload precisely:\n\n  a commit is still a sequential APPEND, so it inherits the whole 244x advantage\n  size becomes proportional to the number of DISTINCT KEYS, not the number of writes\n  it is a topic, so it gets ISR replication and leader election with no new machinery\n  recovery is a log replay, and compaction is what makes that replay bounded",
   "originalText": "This gives a key-value store built out of the log - and it fits the offset workload precisely:\n\n  a commit is still a sequential APPEND, so it inherits the whole 244x advantage\n  size becomes proportional to the number of DISTINCT KEYS, not the number of writes\n  it is a topic, so it gets ISR replication and leader election with no new machinery\n  recovery is a log replay, and compaction is what makes that replay bounded",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 800,
   "width": 535,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100074,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700518,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The elegance: the system reuses its own primitive to store its own\nstate. A database table would be the right SHAPE and would make\nevery commit a random write - forfeiting the sequential advantage\nthe whole design is built on.",
   "originalText": "The elegance: the system reuses its own primitive to store its own\nstate. A database table would be the right SHAPE and would make\nevery commit a random write - forfeiting the sequential advantage\nthe whole design is built on.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "kl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1010,
   "y": 386,
   "width": 490,
   "height": 20,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100075,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700525,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why __consumer_offsets is keyed on group_id ALONE",
   "originalText": "Why __consumer_offsets is keyed on group_id ALONE",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "key",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1010,
   "y": 420,
   "width": 660,
   "height": 50,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100076,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700532,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "key_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "key_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1018,
   "y": 436,
   "width": 644,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100077,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700539,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "partition = hash(group_id) % 50",
   "originalText": "partition = hash(group_id) % 50",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "key",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "kn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1010,
   "y": 490,
   "width": 600,
   "height": 113,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100078,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700546,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "All of a group's offsets live in ONE partition - the same partition whose\nleader hosts that group's coordinator. Three things fall out at once:\n\n  a coordinator reads only ITS OWN partition to recover a group\n  finding the coordinator needs no lookup service: hash the group name\n  a group's commits are TOTALLY ORDERED, which is what makes the\n  generation-ID fencing meaningful - a stale commit is unambiguously stale",
   "originalText": "All of a group's offsets live in ONE partition - the same partition whose\nleader hosts that group's coordinator. Three things fall out at once:\n\n  a coordinator reads only ITS OWN partition to recover a group\n  finding the coordinator needs no lookup service: hash the group name\n  a group's commits are TOTALLY ORDERED, which is what makes the\n  generation-ID fencing meaningful - a stale commit is unambiguously stale",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "kn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1010,
   "y": 660,
   "width": 640,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100079,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700553,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Keying on (group_id, topic, partition) instead would spread one group's offsets\nacross all 50 partitions, forcing a coordinator to read every partition on\nrecovery AND destroying the ordering that fencing relies on. Key selection is\ndoing the same load-bearing work as shard-key selection in a database.",
   "originalText": "Keying on (group_id, topic, partition) instead would spread one group's offsets\nacross all 50 partitions, forcing a coordinator to read every partition on\nrecovery AND destroying the ordering that fencing relies on. Key selection is\ndoing the same load-bearing work as shard-key selection in a database.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "kn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1010,
   "y": 764,
   "width": 487,
   "height": 18,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100080,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700560,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why the cluster map canNOT also be a compacted topic",
   "originalText": "Why the cluster map canNOT also be a compacted topic",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "kn4",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1010,
   "y": 790,
   "width": 648,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100081,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700567,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Bootstrapping. The map tells you which broker leads which partition - storing it\nin a partition means needing the map to find the map. And it needs linearizable\nconsensus with leader election and ephemeral sessions, which ISR replication\ngives durability for but not 'exactly one controller, and everyone agrees who'.",
   "originalText": "Bootstrapping. The map tells you which broker leads which partition - storing it\nin a partition means needing the map to find the map. And it needs linearizable\nconsensus with leader election and ephemeral sessions, which ISR replication\ngives durability for but not 'exactly one controller, and everyone agrees who'.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
 ],
 "appState": {
  "viewBackgroundColor": "#ffffff"
 },
 "files": {}
}